.omo/senpi-task/children/st_01a029e8/sessions/st_01a029e8/2026-08-22T14-33-03-341Z_01a029e3-b26d-717a-b89f-c1accd6f47c2.jsonl:32:{"type":"message","id":"2ec587a3","parentId":"bd00f4ef","timestamp":"2026-08-22T14:33:30.707Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-b3529a4b-8c86-46c4-8c84-c3f38c9e6f21-22|fc_b49724f5-ebbf-919c-b5c9-ae813f6a54c6_3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# New-Tab Menu & Agents Feature

Date: 2026-08-22
Status: Implemented, verified (see Verification below)

## What was built

### 1. Tab-bar "+" popover — Orca parity
Clicking "+" in the tab bar opens the new-tab menu matching Orca's layout:

| Row | Shortcut | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| New Terminal | ⌘T | Opens a terminal tab (existing) |
| New Browser Tab | ⌘⇧B | Opens a browser tab (existing) |
| New Markdown | ⌘⇧M | Opens a "Markdown" tab: self-contained split editor + live preview (no external deps), loaded via data URL |
| New Mobile Emulator | ⌘⌥⇧E | Opens a browser tab sized 390×844 via `cmd_browser_set_bounds` |
| AGENTS group | — | One row per available+enabled agent; click spawns a terminal tab and runs the agent command in it |
| Agent settings… | — | Opens the Settings dialog on the Agents section |

Note: the "Antigravity" row from Orca is intentionally omitted (Orca-specific third-party product integration).

### 2. Agents settings panel
New **Agents** tab in the Settings dialog:
- **Default Agent**: Auto / None / one button per detected agent.
- **Installed [N detected]** with Refresh button (re-runs detection).
- Per agent: Detected/Not-detected badge, Enabled/Disabled toggle (greyed when not detected), expandable Command / Arguments override inputs (mono font), persisted to `localStorage` key `ferryx.agents.v1`.
- Candidates detected on PATH: claude, codex, gemini, opencode, aider, cursor-agent, droid, crush.

### 3. Backend
New Rust command `cmd_agents_detect(names) -> [{ name, available }]` (`src-tauri/src/ipc/agents.rs`) checks PATH availability via `which`; registered in the invoke handler.

## Files touched
- `ui/src/components/NewTabPopover.tsx`, `TabBar.tsx`, `TerminalSplitView.tsx` (prop plumbing)
- `ui/src/App.tsx` (markdown scratch page constant, mobile emulator sizing, agent launch: spawn terminal → write command into PTY, detection on mount)
- `ui/src/lib/agentsSettings.ts` (+ tests): persistence & merge helpers
- `ui/src/components/SettingsDialog.tsx`: Agents tab
- `src-tauri/src/ipc/agents.rs`, `ipc/mod.rs`, `lib.rs`: detection command

## Verification
- `cargo test --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml`: 162 passed / 0 failed
- `cargo clippy --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean
- `bun run --cwd ui build`: exit 0
- Frontend suite: related suites all green (agentsSettings 7, SettingsDialog 14, NewTabPopover 9, TabBar 13, App 18); see run output for totals. Pre-existing failures in `terminalHostManager.test.tsx` (5) are unrelated to this feature.

## 2026-08-22 Runtime Regression Fixes

### Input-only new-tab popover
- Root cause: the new-tab trigger and absolute popover were nested inside the horizontal `role=tablist` scroller (`overflow-x-auto`). CSS overflow clipping hid everything below the search input.
- Fix: move the trigger/popover outside the overflow container while retaining it inside the tab strip `SortableContext`.
- Regression test: `TabBar.test.tsx` asserts the New tab trigger is not a descendant of the tablist overflow container.
- User manually confirmed the full menu is now visible.
- Follow-up UX decision: the search/URL input and submit behavior were removed. The `+` popover now opens directly as an action-and-agent menu.

### Stable development launch and HMR
- Root `package.json` had been overwritten by an unrelated Electron/Orca package and lost the `tauri` script.
- Restored Ferryx scripts (`bun tauri dev` → `cargo tauri dev`) and added `devRuntimeContract.test.ts` to lock the script, `127.0.0.1:5173` dev URL, strict Vite port, and HMR alignment.

### PTY exhaustion after session restore
- Symptom: `PTY_CREATION_ERROR ... Device not configured`; macOS had all 511 PTYs allocated.
- Root cause: the restore effect depended on mutable workspace tab/session state. Restoring changed those dependencies, reran the effect, and repeatedly respawned the same persisted terminals. Ferryx created hundreds of zsh children within seconds.
- Fixes:
  - restore only once per continuously active project;
  - serialize only terminal sessions referenced by tabs/panes;
  - drop stale orphan sessions during deserialization;
  - preserve legacy `layout.layoutsByTabId` split-pane references while filtering orphans.
- Regression coverage: repeated restore effect, orphan serialization/deserialization, legacy split-pane restore.
- Verification: PTYs returned from 511 to 52 after shutting down the faulty app; focused tests 50/50 pass and the production UI build succeeds.

### Flush terminal pane layout
- Replaced 6px split handles (which visibly separated terminal surfaces) with layout-neutral 1px gray dividers (`border` token).
- Preserved a wider invisible pointer hit area around each 1px line, so resizing remains usable without a visible gap.
- Filled the complete terminal host surface with the active xterm theme background. Any leftover pixels below the final fitted xterm row now blend into the terminal instead of appearing as a black bottom strip.
- Regression tests cover horizontal/vertical 1px dividers, invisible resize hit targets, active theme background fill, and existing pointer-drag resize behavior.

### Terminal first-paint and bottom-strip color
- Root cause: the tab bar and terminal layout wrappers used the shared `--terminal` CSS token (`#0a0a0a`) while xterm rendered with the selected terminal theme background (`#282c34`). The mismatch produced a temporary black active-tab flash and exposed a black strip in pixels left below the final xterm row.
- The default `--terminal` and `--terminal-rgb` values now match the default xterm theme before React mounts.
- The last resolved terminal background is cached in `ferryx.terminal.background` and applied in `main.tsx` before the initial React render.
- Native/Ghostty preference resolution updates both CSS terminal tokens and the cache, keeping the active tab, terminal wrappers, and xterm canvas on the same color.
- Terminal paint/settings tests: 30/30 pass; frontend production build succeeds.

